  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BNR consultancy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to address the Build-Neglect-Repair (BNR) cycle in global water infrastructure, a persistent issue highlighted in the 2017 report on Dutch development aid by the Policy and Operations Evaluation Department (IOB) of the Dutch Ministry of Foreign Affairs.Funded by the Partner for Water (PfW) programme under the Netherlands Enterprise Agency (RVO), the project seeks to engage Dutch and international stakeholders in developing sustainable solutions for water infrastructure maintenance.Key activities include stakeholder mapping and analysis, conducting a political, social, and economic analysis, drafting a communication and advocacy strategy, facilitating stakeholder dialogues, and advising on Operation and Maintenance (O&amp;M)-based design principles.The project&apos;s ultimate goal is to enhance international collaboration, raise awareness, and promote sustainable asset management practices, thereby contributing to the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). The consultancy runs from mid-August 2024 to February 2025.</narrative>
  </description>
